You know, work that doesn't involve a lot of thought, but you know, simple work that needs to get done. There is one final idea on how we can fight distractions, and it is counterintuitive. Gloria says we can increase our capacity for focus if we consciously take breaks from the things we are focusing on. There is a Japanese expression that's called Yohaku nobi, which means the beauty of empty space. And there's a very well-known Japanese garden in Kyoto,

69
00:45:16.000 --> 00:45:57.000
which has the most beautiful rocks that are very carefully positioned. And what is as important as the rocks themselves is the space around the rocks because that space creates a kind of dynamism that makes these rocks more beautiful. And we can use that as a metaphor to think about our work day. So, of course, we want to perform the best that we possibly can. But we also have to design empty space into our day to enable our work to shine.

